Source landscape note: the 2023 Brazil/Lula 1B universe is dominated by official Brazilian foreign-affairs, defense, and security texts on disarmament, nonproliferation, nuclear-energy safety, the nuclear-powered submarine program, and cyber/critical-infrastructure risk policy, with a smaller layer of technical international material from the IAEA, CTBTO, ABACC, SIPRI, and specialist scholarship. I found both restraint-facing and capability-facing documents, plus several paywalled or metadata-only research leads that are worth preserving for later inspection.

